QuestGuidance.Register("en",207,{
[6593]="70008B59\n1\tTalk to Sigrun\tThe dwarves Sigrun and Greip were sent north of Glóin's camp in the Western Bruinen Source to scout Helegrod and have likely established a small camp among the trees in sight of the Bitter Stair. Glóin has sent you to speak with the scouts he dispatched to watch the Bitter Stair that climbs to the gates of Helegrod, far to the north of his Western Bruinen Source camp.\n2\tComplete Ancient Foes of the Spider-bane\030Complete The Extent of the Threat\030Complete Old Friendships\030Complete The Worm-hunter's Lament\tThe dwarves Sigrun and Greip have several friends they need to consult and send information to before they venture back into Helegrod.\n3\tFind the entrance to Helegrod\tHelegrod is north-east of Sigrun and Greip's camp. It is now time for you to see this ancient fortress for yourself.\n",
[6594]="70024530\n1\tTalk to Fenric Banks in Oatbarton\tFenric Banks is in Oatbarton, the hobbit-town in the southern reaches of Evendim. It is one of the most northerly villages of the Shire. Barliman Butterbur has asked you to investigate the worries of the hobbit Fenric Banks, in Oatbarton.\n2\tTalk to Bounder Boffin inside Northcotton Farm\tThe Northcotton Farm is located west of Oatbarton's town centre and up the steep hill. Fenric Banks has told you of the hobbit disappearances and wants you to gather a couple friends and investigate the Northcotton Farm, where one of the hobbits was last seen.\n",
[6595]="700246F2\n1\tTravel to Sâri-surma and make your way through the fortress\tDrugoth the Deathmonger has been commanded to raise an army of wights on Sâri-surma, in Forochel. Elrond has translated the broken tablet he found within the Lost Temple and now knows the location of another Gaunt-lord.\n2\tTalk to Pirita in the fortress on Sâri-surma\tPirita of the Lossoth is inside the fortress on Sâri-surma. Pirita wishes to speak with you.\n",
[6596]="700246F3\n1\tTalk to Yrjänä in Sâri-surma\tYrjänä is somewhere within the fortress on Sâri-surma. Pirita has asked you to find the Lossoth chieftain, Yrjänä, within the depths of the fortress.\n",
[6597]="700246F4\n1\tDefeat Drugoth the Death-monger in the fortress on Sâri-surma\tDrugoth the Death-monger waits in the depths of his fortress on Sâri-surma. Yrjänä has told you that Drugoth acts impulsively, more like an animal than a thinking being.\n2\tTalk to Yrjänä\tYrjänä wants to speak with you now that you have defeated Drugoth in the fortress on Sâri-surma.\n",
[6598]="700246F5\n1\tFind Gortheron's lair in the south-western reaches of the Lich Bluffs, in Enedwaith\tThe stronghold of Gortheron the Doom-caller is located in Enedwaith, in the south-western reaches of the Lich Bluffs. Yrjänä found a tablet in the depths of the fortress on Sâri-surma that reveals the location of the leader of the Gaunt-lords.\n",
[6599]="70024717\n1\tSurvive the wages of war and conquer your fear in the east wing\030Survive the spread of plague and poison in the west wing\tOst Dunhoth has two wings that must be explored before the central area can be unsealed.\n2\tTalk to Túgonn\tTúgonn is in the entrance of Ost Dunhoth. You have conquered two wings of Ost Dunhoth and should return now to Túgonn.\n",
[6600]="70024718\n1\tFight through Ost Dunhoth and defeat Gortheron\tThe central area of Ost Dunhoth is open.\n2\tTúgonn is in the entrance of Ost Dunhoth.\t\n",
[6601]="70024540\n1\tBounder Boffin's assistant Tulip is somewhere further inside the Northcotton Farm, and it could be the missing hobbits are as well. Bounder Boffin has asked you to search for the missing hobbits inside the Northcotton Farm.\t\n2\tTalk to Tulip Grubb within the Northcotton Farm\tTulip Grubb is somewhere within the Northcotton Farm. You have rescued the missing hobbits and should now find Bounder Boffin's assistant, Tulip Grubb, who came into the farm to investigate the disappearances.\n",
[6602]="70024551\n1\tDefeat Thadúr the Ravager on the Northcotton Farm\tTulip Grubb told you about an evil-looking creature named Thadúr at the end of the path through the doors behind Tulip. He seems to be the creature responsible for the deadly Darkthorn poison. You and your allies need to defeat Thadúr before he can bring any more trouble to the Shire.\n2\tTalk to Bounder Boffin on the Northcotton Farm\tBounder Boffin is inside the Northcotton Farm. You have defeated Thadúr the Ravager, and Bounder Boffin is eager to speak with you about your victory on the Northcotton Farm.\n",
[6603]="7002468E\n1\tTalk to Ronald Dwale about Thadúr's final words\tRonald Dwale lives north-east of Oatbarton, just outside the village of Dwaling. Bounder Boffin has sent you to speak with Ronald Dwale about Thadúr's final words. If anyone knows what Tirith dan Forduath is, he will.\n2\tTalk to Benedric Jacklin in the town of Stoneheight\tStoneheight is located on the North Downs, north-east of Amon Raith. The town of Stoneheight is located atop a sloping rise north of a deserted farm-house. Ronald Dwale has teased apart the meaning of Thadúr's final words and has told you that Tirith dan Forduath was the ancient name for a place now called Stoneheight, on the North Downs.\n",
[6604]="70024691\n1\tSearch Stoneheight for survivors of the attack\tBenedric Jacklin has asked you to search further within Stoneheight for survivors of the attack. The town of Stoneheight was attacked by a merciless figure who moved with a single-minded purpose, and now you must search for survivors.\n2\tTalk to Seward Pearse before he succumbs to his injuries\tYou have found a survivor of the attack on Stoneheight, but his wounds seem very severe.\n",
[6605]="70024693\n1\tSearch further within Stoneheight for sign of the helm\tSeward Pearse's home is further within the town of Stoneheight, and he wants you to see if the helm is still there. Ivar the Blood-hand stalked through the town of Stoneheight, and Seward Pearse believes he came looking for the helm Seward purchased from a merchant.\n2\tWhile in the wreckage of the town of Stoneheight, you saw in-fighting between two of the enemies left by Ivar to finish the job. Dale Truitt slew Búbhosh-grat and now must be defeated if the people of Stoneheight are to rebuild.\t\n3\tTalk to Benedric Jacklin in Stoneheight\tBenedric Jacklin wishes to speak with you about what happened to the town of Stoneheight.\n",
[6606]="70024699\n1\tBring the broken tablet to Elrond in Rivendell\tElrond Half-elven is in his library in Rivendell. You have been given a mysterious tablet that was found in the town of Stoneheight. The tablet is covered in mysterious runes; perhaps Elrond can read them.\n2\tFind Ithriel at the Lost Temple\tThe Elf-scout Ithriel is scouting the Lost Temple, located at Ost Chall in the northern reaches of Nan Tornaeth. Elrond has read the runes on the tablet found in Stoneheight, and a mention of the Lost Temple has drawn his notice.\n",
[6607]="7002469A\n1\tCross the temple-grounds and enter the crypts\tThe crypts of the Lost Temple are beyond the grounds of the temple. Ithriel has asked you to fight the mercenary band hired by Ferndúr as you make your way across the temple-grounds.\n2\tTalk to Scristan\tThe mercenary Scristan is seriously injured just within the entrance to the crypts of the Lost Temple. You have found an injured mercenary, but he makes no hostile sign.\n",
[6608]="7002469B\n1\tDefeat Ferndúr the Virulent within the Lost Temple\tFerndúr the Virulent is further within the crypts of the Lost Temple. The mercenary Scristan believes that the Gaunt-lord intended to throw away the lives of the mercenary band he hired, and Scristan wants him to pay for it.\n2\tTalk to Elrond in the depths of the Lost Temple\tElrond wishes to speak with you about your defeat of Ferndúr the Virulent. You have defeated the Gaunt-lord Ferndúr in the depths of the Lost Temple, and now Elrond wishes to speak with you.\n",
[6609]="70037CE8\n1\tThane Edric's men can be found inside Entwade, as well as along the road west to Middlemead and among the fields outside southern Entwade. Thane Edric has asked that you aid his men in identifying and minimizing the threats that lurk outside Entwade, as well as helping the men of the settlement bolster its defences before the White Hand returns to siege the town.\t\n2\tTalk to Thane Edric\tThane Edric can be found in the Mead Hall of Entwade in eastern Kingstead. You have aided Thane Edric's men greatly in preparing the town and eliminating the Enemy's nearest forces.\n",
[6610]="70009E5A\n1\tTalk to Alf\tAlf Earthenway is at Grothum. Alf Earthenway asked you to help him escape from the goblins.\n2\tTalk to Marigold Winterdown\tMarigold Winterdown is at the hobbit-village of Hoarhallow, found on the western edge of the Grimwood Forest in Hithlad. The village is found on the shores of the Hoarwell River. Alf is free, but before he left you, he asked that you inform Marigold Winterdown that he would be returning to work at the bakery in Hoarhallow shortly.\n",
[6611]="70035749\n1\tCyneberg did a great deal of work in Grimnesberg as her grief overwhelmed her. You should have a look around and see where Cyneberg's mind was while she captured this town.\t\n2\tTell Cyneberg what you saw\tCyneberg can be found in the centre of Grimnesberg. You should speak with Cyneberg.\n",
[6612]="7000D720\n1\tTalk to Earth-kin Scout\t\n",
[6613]="7004F919\n1\tDori can be found atop Stánbalk, the Stone Wall. You have found evidence that Nori has gone into Thikil-gundu, and Dori now seeks to find his brother before Karazgar or the mysterious dwarf-wights can bring any harm to him. NOTE: You must complete the instance 'Thikil-gundu' on its solo difficulty to advance this quest.\t\n2\tDori and Nori can be found in the Keep of Tharrazhâr. You have repelled Karazgar and rescued Nori from the depths of Thikil-gundu, but many mysteries linger about the fate of the Steel Keep. You should talk to Dori and Nori.\t\n",
[6614]="70050A88\n1\tTalk to Dori in Thikil-gundu\tDori can be found in Thikil-gundu. If you have become separated, you may call him and the rest of the company by using your horn. You have come to Thikil-gundu in search of Nori. You should now speak to Dori in Thikil-gundu.\n2\tTalk to Dori\030Search the hoarding-vault of Immêsh-khalt\tThe hoarding-vault of Immêsh-khalt can be found in the centre of Durûz-mazal, the Chamber of Faces. Dori has directed you and the rest of the company to search the hoarding-vault of Immêsh-khalt for signs of Nori.\n3\tFind a way into the smithies of Kall-khebâb\tThe smithies of Kall-khebâb can be found in the eastern halls of Thikil-gundu. Determined to delve deeper into Thikil-gundu, Dori has asked you to find the smithies of Kall-khebâb so that you might gain passage into the other halls of the Steel Keep.\n4\tDefeat Karkasht Crow-feeder and the Orcs of Gundabad in Kall-khebâb\tKarkasht Crow-feeder can be found in the smithies of Kall-khebâb. You have discovered a massive hobgoblin leading the Orcs in the smithies of Kall-khebâb. You must defeat him if you are to continue deeper into Thikil-gundu.\n5\tTalk to Dori at the ruined hall to Afhân-binnîn in Kall-khebâb\030Find the northern hall that leads into Afhân-binnîn from Kall-khebâb\tA hall to Afhân-binnîn can be found at the northern end of the smithies of Kall-khebâb. With the smithies clear of foes, you should now search the smithies for a way into the lore-trove of Afhân-binnîn.\n6\tFind a way to Afhân-binnîn through the feast-house of Amrâg-zahar\tThe feast-house of Amrâg-zahar can be found through the northernmost doors of Durûz-mazal, the Chamber of Faces. With the heat of the smithies now spreading through Thikil-gundu, Dori hopes to find another way to reach Afhân-binnîn and continue the search for Nori.\n7\tTalk to Dori in Afhân-binnîn\030Search for Nori in Afhân-binnîn\tNori might be found somewhere within Afhân-binnîn. Afhân-binnîn can be found through Amrâg-zahar. You have discovered a passage into Afhân-binnîn, and you should now search for Nori within the lore-troves of Thikil-gundu.\n8\tDefeat Frór the Lost and banish the fell spirit inhabiting his remains\030Recover the crown of Dáin\tFrór the Lost can be found in the heights of Afhân-binnîn. You have discovered the remains of Frór, son of Dáin I, brought to life by a fell spirit in Afhân-binnîn. You should defeat him and let him at last be laid to rest.\n9\tDeliver the crown of Dáin to Dori in Thikil-gundu\tDori can be found in Thikil-gundu. You have defeated the fell spirit inhabiting the remains of Frór and recovered the long-lost crown of Dáin. You should offer the crown to Dori and learn what is to be done.\n10\tSearch for Nori at Thikil-nesad, the Steel Seat\tThikil-nesad, the Steel Seat, can be found deep within Thikil-gundu. Fearing that Nori has been discovered by the inhabitants of the Steel Keep, Dori now hopes to find him before the old throne of Thikil-gundu.\n11\tDefeat Athramóth\tAthramóth and her brood can be found in Thikil-nesad. You have discovered a great cold-drake resting among her brood. You should defeat Athramóth and make safe the old throne of the Steel Keep.\n12\tTalk to Nori at Thikil-nesad\tNori can be found at Thikil-nesad. Nori has fled into Thikil-nesad and unwittingly reunited with Dori. You should talk to Nori.\n13\tTalk to Dori in Thikil-gundu\tDori can be found in Thikil-gundu. You have reunited with Nori. You should now speak to Dori and learn what is to be done.\n14\tFind a way through Amrâg-zahar to Zashar-tûmun\tZashar-tûmun, the ruin-dwellings of Thikil-gundu, can be found to the west of the feast-house of Amrâg-zahar. Nori has warned you that Karazgar now prepares a great force of dragon-kind in Zashar-tûmun. You should find a way to Zashar-tûmun and confront Karazgar.\n15\tFind and confront Karazgar in Zashar-tûmun\tKarazgar can be found somewhere within Zashar-tûmun. Nori has warned you that Karazgar now prepares a great force of dragon-kind in Zashar-tûmun. You should find and confront Karazgar.\n16\tDefeat Karazgar, the Weeping Warrior\tKarazgar can be found in the western reaches of Zashar-tûmun. You have found Karazgar, the Weeping Warrior, and you should now attempt to defeat him.\n17\tTalk to Dori in Thikil-gundu\tDori can be found in Thikil-gundu. If you have become separated, you may call him and the rest of the company by using your horn. You have repelled Karazgar and rescued Nori from the depths of Thikil-gundu. You should now speak to Dori.\n",
[6615]="70051610\n1\tTalk to Dori in Thikil-gundu\tDori can be found in Thikil-gundu. If you have become separated, you may call him and the rest of the company by using your horn. You have come to Thikil-gundu in search of Nori. You should now speak to Dori in Thikil-gundu.\n2\tTalk to Dori\030Search the hoarding-vault of Immêsh-khalt\tThe hoarding-vault of Immêsh-khalt can be found in the centre of Durûz-mazal, the Chamber of Faces. Dori has directed you and the rest of the company to search the hoarding-vault of Immêsh-khalt for signs of Nori.\n3\tFind a way into the smithies of Kall-khebâb\tThe smithies of Kall-khebâb can be found in the eastern halls of Thikil-gundu. Determined to delve deeper into Thikil-gundu, Dori has asked you to find the smithies of Kall-khebâb so that you might gain passage into the other halls of the Steel Keep.\n4\tDefeat Karkasht Crow-feeder and the Orcs of Gundabad in Kall-khebâb\tKarkasht Crow-feeder can be found in the smithies of Kall-khebâb. You have discovered a massive hobgoblin leading the Orcs in the smithies of Kall-khebâb. You must defeat him if you are to continue deeper into Thikil-gundu.\n5\tTalk to Dori at the ruined hall to Afhân-binnîn in Kall-khebâb\030Find the northern hall that leads into Afhân-binnîn from Kall-khebâb\tA hall to Afhân-binnîn can be found at the northern end of the smithies of Kall-khebâb. With the smithies clear of foes, you should now search the smithies for a way into the lore-trove of Afhân-binnîn.\n6\tFind a way to Afhân-binnîn through the feast-house of Amrâg-zahar\tThe feast-house of Amrâg-zahar can be found through the northernmost doors of Durûz-mazal, the Chamber of Faces. With the heat of the smithies now spreading through Thikil-gundu, Dori hopes to find another way to reach Afhân-binnîn and continue the search for Nori.\n7\tTalk to Dori in Afhân-binnîn\030Search for Nori in Afhân-binnîn\tNori might be found somewhere within Afhân-binnîn. Afhân-binnîn can be found through Amrâg-zahar. You have discovered a passage into Afhân-binnîn, and you should now search for Nori within the lore-troves of Thikil-gundu.\n8\tDefeat Frór the Lost and banish the fell spirit inhabiting his remains\030Recover the crown of Dáin\tFrór the Lost can be found in the heights of Afhân-binnîn. You have discovered the remains of Frór, son of Dáin I, brought to life by a fell spirit in Afhân-binnîn. You should defeat him and let him at last be laid to rest.\n9\tDeliver the crown of Dáin to Dori in Thikil-gundu\tDori can be found in Thikil-gundu. You have defeated the fell spirit inhabiting the remains of Frór and recovered the long-lost crown of Dáin. You should offer the crown to Dori and learn what is to be done.\n10\tSearch for Nori at Thikil-nesad, the Steel Seat\tThikil-nesad, the Steel Seat, can be found deep within Thikil-gundu. Fearing that Nori has been discovered by the inhabitants of the Steel Keep, Dori now hopes to find him before the old throne of Thikil-gundu.\n11\tDefeat Athramóth\tAthramóth and her brood can be found in Thikil-nesad. You have discovered a great cold-drake resting among her brood. You should defeat Athramóth and make safe the old throne of the Steel Keep.\n12\tTalk to Nori at Thikil-nesad\tNori can be found at Thikil-nesad. Nori has fled into Thikil-nesad and unwittingly reunited with Dori. You should talk to Nori.\n13\tTalk to Dori in Thikil-gundu\tDori can be found in Thikil-gundu. You have reunited with Nori. You should now speak to Dori and learn what is to be done.\n14\tFind a way through Amrâg-zahar to Zashar-tûmun\tZashar-tûmun, the ruin-dwellings of Thikil-gundu, can be found to the west of the feast-house of Amrâg-zahar. Nori has warned you that Karazgar now prepares a great force of dragon-kind in Zashar-tûmun. You should find a way to Zashar-tûmun and confront Karazgar.\n15\tFind and confront Karazgar in Zashar-tûmun\tKarazgar can be found somewhere within Zashar-tûmun. Nori has warned you that Karazgar now prepares a great force of dragon-kind in Zashar-tûmun. You should find and confront Karazgar.\n16\tDefeat Karazgar, the Weeping Warrior\tKarazgar can be found in the western reaches of Zashar-tûmun. You have found Karazgar, the Weeping Warrior, and you should now attempt to defeat him.\n17\tTalk to Dori in Thikil-gundu\tDori can be found in Thikil-gundu. If you have become separated, you may call him and the rest of the company by using your horn. You have repelled Karazgar and rescued Nori from the depths of Thikil-gundu. You should now speak to Dori.\n",
[6616]="700379DA\n1\tThane Edric and his wife, Léoflad, can be found outside the Mead Hall of Entwade. Thane Edric has asked you to aid Léoflad and his people as they make ready to travel. You should speak to Edric and Léoflad.\t\n2\tTalk to Thane Edric\tThane Edric can be found outside the Mead Hall of Entwade near the waggons. You have aided the people of Entwade greatly, and should now speak to Thane Edric of what is to be done next.\n",
[6617]="7005B187\n1\tDestroy banners of the Ufúrzrak at Muru Azog\tBanners of the Ufúrzrak clan can be found at Muru Azog, before the East-gate of Nud-mekhem at Azanulbizar. You should destroy the banners of the Ufúrzrak.\n2\tDestroy banners of the Ufúrzrak at Muru Azog (total: 8)\tBanners of the Ufúrzrak clan can be found at Muru Azog, before the East-gate of Nud-mekhem at Azanulbizar. You should destroy the banners of the Ufúrzrak.\n3\tCompleted\tYou have destroyed many banners of the Ufúrzrak at Muru Azog.\n",
[6618]="7001ABE9\n1\tDeliver the tough vines to Buckley Sheppard\030Collect tough vines from the Old Forest (total: 20)\tRoots can be found throughout the Old Forest in the eastern stretches to the north and south of Adso's camp. Buckley Sheppard is at Adso's camp, along the Great East Road. Buckley Sheppard has offered to pay you for finding tough vines from the roots in the Old Forest. The vines will be used to make tough strappings to use in place of nails.\n",
[6619]="7004DA3C\n1\tDefeat Orc-kind in Eryn Lasgalen (total: 12)\tOrcs can be found scattered throughout Eryn Lasgalen. King Thranduil has bade you defeat any Orc-kind you come across.\n2\tCompleted\tDefeated many Orc-kind in Eryn Lasgalen.\n",
[6620]="7002729B\n1\tComplete Mystery of the Trees\030Complete Baa, Baa, Black Sheep\030Complete Dimming the Lights\030Complete Spirits of Dunland\tAndreg is near the Slade of Shadows, south of the Rohirrim scout-camp. Andreg has asked you to help him face the evils at the Slade of Shadows.\n2\tTalk to Andreg near the Slade of Shadows\tAndreg is near the Slade of Shadows, south of the Rohirrim scout-camp. You should return to Andreg with news of your successes.\n",
[6621]="7002C776\n1\tVisit the Rohirrim-camp along the northern base of the Cuthstan\tThe Rohirrim-camp may be found along the road north of the Cuthstan, to the west of Stangard. Byrnstan has asked you to visit Frithstan and ask about the delay in his report to Stangard.\n2\tTalk to Penda about Frithstan's location\tPenda may be found in the Rohirrim-camp along the road north of the Cuthstan, to the west of Stangard. Penda seems to be the only man left at Frithstan's camp.\n",
[6622]="700686A5\n1\tComplete 'The Scourge's Captains'\030Complete 'Stealing From Their Own'\030Complete 'Heirs To Naught'\tEshmun, Captain of the Haven, can be found at the Harbour-warden's Tower in the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl. Eshmun, Captain of the Haven, has asked for your aid in ridding Umbar Baharbêl of those still loyal to Balakhôr the Scourge and the Heirs of Castamir.\n2\tTalk to Eshmun at the Harbour-warden's Tower\tEshmun, Captain of the Haven, can be found at the Harbour-warden's Tower in the Sail-haven of Umbar Baharbêl. You have done much to rout the remnants of the Heirs of Castamir in the Sail-haven. You should talk to Eshmun.\n",
[6623]="700479E3\n1\tParticipate in Yule Festival activities in Frostbluff (total: 10)\tEvery day there is something to do in Frostbluff. Every day there is Yule! Come and join everyone in Frostbluff and participate in many Yule Festival activities!\n2\tSpeak to Mara Sandydowns\tMara Sandydowns would like to thank you for your participation in the Yule Festival today.\n",
[6624]="7004C990\n1\tParticipate in Yule Festival activities in Frostbluff (total: 10)\tEvery day there is something to do in Frostbluff. Every day there is Yule! Come and join everyone in Frostbluff and participate in many Yule Festival activities!\n2\tSpeak to Mara Sandydowns\tMara Sandydowns would like to thank you for your participation in the Yule Festival today.\n",
